luated; after any later mutation it is stale. Submit only when you choose to finish. The trajectory permits at most 8 model calls. Action catalog: [{\"action\":\"tree\",\"description\":\"List files below one workspace-relative path.\",\"parameters\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"maxLength\":512,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"],\"type\":\"object\"}},{\"action\":\"search\",\"description\":\"Find literal UTF-8 text below one workspace-relative path.\",\"parameters\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"maxLength\":512,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"query\":{\"maxLength\":500,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"query\"],\"type\":\"object\"}},{\"action\":\"read\",\"description\":\"Read one complete UTF-8 workspace file.\",\"parameters\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"maxLength\":512,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"],\"type\":\"object\"}},{\"action\":\"patch\",\"description\":\"Replace one exact string in one mutable file. The old text must occur exactly once and the expected hash must be current.\",\"parameters\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"expected_file_sha256\":{\"pattern\":\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"new\":{\"maxLength\":32768,\"type\":\"string\"},\"old\":{\"maxLength\":32768,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"path\":{\"maxLength\":512,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"old\",\"new\",\"expected_file_sha256\"],\"type\":\"object\"}},{\"action\":\"replace_file\",\"description\":\"Replace one complete mutable UTF-8 file using its current file hash.\",\"parameters\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"content\":{\"maxLength\":32768,\"type\":\"string\"},\"expected_file_sha256\":{\"pattern\":\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"path\":{\"maxLength\":512,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"content\",\"expected_file_sha256\"],\"type\":\"object\"}},{\"action\":\"run_check\",\"description\":\"Run one declared visible check against the exact current candidate.\",\"parameters\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"check_id\":{\"maxLength\":100,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"check_id\"],\"type\":\"object\"}},{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"description\":\"Reopen one exact externally custodied result by its receipt ID.\",\"parameters\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"result_id\":{\"maxLength\":100,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"result_id\"],\"type\":\"object\"}},{\"action\":\"submit\",\"description\":\"Submit the exact current candidate and a bounded final response.\",\"parameters\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"final_response\":{\"maxLength\":12000,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"final_response\"],\"type\":\"object\"}}]<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nAUTHORITATIVE TASK\nFix `planDeploymentWaves` according to `docs/deployment-waves.md`. The intended implementation target is `src/deployment-waves.mjs`, and the visible tests are in `test/deployment-waves.test.mjs`. Preserve the public API and the behavior of the other exported helpers. Do not weaken or edit tests, documentation, package metadata, or repository instructions. Run `npm test` before you finish.\n\nYour final response must contain these exact labels in this order, with substantive content after each label:\n\nRoot cause:\nFiles changed:\nVerification:\nRemaining limitations:\n\n\n\nINITIAL EXACT WORK SURFACE\n{\"candidate_id\":\"2fc2be00c2187276656bd1cade8253893a6b784ac98e6df87ee36f8075d335bb\",\"cell_id\":\"D5\",\"exact_external_history\":true,\"exact_results_reopenable_after_demotion\":true,\"mutable_paths\":[\"src/deployment-waves.mjs\"],\"schema_version\":\"capability-terrain-initial-surface-v0\",\"visible_check_id\":\"npm_test\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"tree\",\"path\":\".\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nEXACT ACTION RESULT\n{\"accepted\":true,\"candidate_id\":\"2fc2be00c2187276656bd1cade8253893a6b784ac98e6df87ee36f8075d335bb\",\"entries\":[{\"bytes\":345,\"path\":\"AGENTS.md\",\"sha256\":\"56a7b8166f1bced4445f3050f1a1ea04f2bbc593ea13ff122ac2c8b5dd90cb3c\",\"type\":\"file\"},{\"path\":\"docs\",\"type\":\"directory\"},{\"bytes\":2714,\"path\":\"docs/deployment-waves.md\",\"sha256\":\"34ffbb756b7099c9eef6ace4e46de5c1134ea73c2bf2d82e7e273285961ac416\",\"type\":\"file\"},{\"bytes\":173,\"path\":\"package.json\",\"sha256\":\"ac0bd632ac16c529000e10a57dea87d26b4fd1fd2d2d1b77b071fa210c010be1\",\"type\":\"file\"},{\"bytes\":162,\"path\":\"README.md\",\"sha256\":\"91d60f89f822f10c2692887e97764a57a89a80333d41421af53e9cf5bc6f2f68\",\"type\":\"file\"},{\"path\":\"src\",\"type\":\"directory\"},{\"bytes\":538,\"path\":\"src/deployment-waves.mjs\",\"sha256\":\"36c42e533176ecbd313f4f4ecff7be81e04e0b4bb19bd9b3bb5908ed88cff285\",\"type\":\"file\"},{\"path\":\"test\",\"type\":\"directory\"},{\"bytes\":1176,\"path\":\"test/deployment-waves.test.mjs\",\"sha256\":\"845674ded7512c907e141fc5299e656b4cb26c3f456b96bc87814741d522998e\",\"type\":\"file\"}],\"path\":\".\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\",\"schema_version\":\"exact-action-result-v0\",\"tool\":\"tree\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read\",\"path\":\"docs/deployment-waves.md\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nEXACT ACTION RESULT\n{\"accepted\":true,\"bytes\":2714,\"candidate_id\":\"2fc2be00c2187276656bd1cade8253893a6b784ac98e6df87ee36f8075d335bb\",\"content\":\"# Deployment-wave contract\\n\\n`planDeploymentWaves(requestedIds, services, options)` builds dependency-safe waves for a requested deployment. It must not mutate any input.\\n\\n## Validation and canonicalization\\n\\n- A canonical string is a string trimmed at both ends and non-empty.\\n- `requestedIds` and `services` must be arrays. Requested IDs are canonicalized and must be unique after trimming.\\n- `options` must be a non-array object when supplied. `maxParallel` is required and must be a positive safe integer.\\n- Every service is validated before requested-membership or dependency-closure filtering. A service is a non-array object with:\\n  - canonical unique `id`;\\n  - `dependsOn`, omitted as `[]` or otherwise an array of canonical IDs unique after trimming;\\n  - optional boolean `enabled` (default `true`);\\n  - optional boolean `alreadyDeployed` (default `false`);\\n  - optional `exclusiveGroup`, either `null`/omitted or a canonical non-empty string;\\n  - optional integer `priority` from `0` through `100` (default `0`).\\n- Every dependency must name a service, and a service cannot depend on itself. Every requested ID must name a service. Invalid data throws `TypeError`, including invalid unrequested services.\\n\\n## Required closure\\n\\nThe required closure begins with requested services and recursively includes their dependencies. An `alreadyDeployed` service satisfies its dependency and appears in `alreadySatisfiedIds`; traversal stops at that service, so its own dependencies are not added. Already-deployed services never appear in waves.\\n\\nAn enabled service may depend on a disabled service only when the disabled service is already deployed. Otherwise a disabled member of the required closure makes the request unschedulable and throws `Error`.\\n\\nA dependency cycle among required, non-deployed services throws `Error`.\\n\\n## Wave construction\\n\\nA service is ready only when every dependency is already deployed or appeared in an earlier wave. Dependencies cannot share a wave with their dependents.\\n\\nFor each wave, sort ready services by descending `priority`, breaking ties by original service-array position. Greedily scan that order and select at most `maxParallel` services. At most one selected service may use any non-null `exclusiveGroup`; skipped ready services remain eligible for the next wave. Null groups do not conflict.\\n\\n## Result\\n\\nReturn a fresh object with properties in exactly this order:\\n\\n1. `requestedIds` — canonical requested IDs in request order\\n2. `includedIds` — all scheduled IDs in wave order\\n3. `alreadySatisfiedIds` — required already-deployed IDs in original service-array order\\n4. `waves` — fresh arrays of canonical service IDs\\n\\nNo returned array may alias an input.\\n\\n\",\"file_sha256\":\"34ffbb756b7099c9eef6ace4e46de5c1134ea73c2bf2d82e7e273285961ac416\",\"path\":\"docs/deployment-waves.md\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-002\",\"schema_version\":\"exact-action-result-v0\",\"tool\":\"read\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read\",\"path\":\"src/deployment-waves.mjs\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nEXACT ACTION RESULT\n{\"accepted\":true,\"bytes\":538,\"candidate_id\":\"2fc2be00c2187276656bd1cade8253893a6b784ac98e6df87ee36f8075d335bb\",\"content\":\"export function listServiceIds(services) {\\n  if (!Array.isArray(services)) throw new TypeError(\\\"services must be an array\\\");\\n  return services.map((service) => service.id);\\n}\\n\\nexport function planDeploymentWaves(requestedIds, services, options) {\\n  return {\\n    requestedIds: [...requestedIds],\\n    includedIds: [...requestedIds],\\n    alreadySatisfiedIds: [],\\n    waves: [[...requestedIds]]\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function describeWave(wave) {\\n  if (!Array.isArray(wave)) throw new TypeError(\\\"wave must be an array\\\");\\n  return wave.join(\\\"+\\\");\\n}\\n\\n\",\"file_sha256\":\"36c42e533176ecbd313f4f4ecff7be81e04e0b4bb19bd9b3bb5908ed88cff285\",\"path\":\"src/deployment-waves.mjs\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-003\",\"schema_version\":\"exact-action-result-v0\",\"tool\":\"read\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read\",\"path\":\"test/deployment-waves.test.mjs\"}\n</think>\n\n{\"action\": \"read\", \"path\": \"test/deployment-waves.test.mjs\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nEXACT ACTION RESULT\n{\"accepted\":false,\"candidate_id\":\"2fc2be00c2187276656bd1cade8253893a6b784ac98e6df87ee36f8075d335bb\",\"error\":{\"code\":\"invalid_json\",\"message\":\"Extra data: line 2 column 1 (char 58)\"},\"result_id\":\"RESULT-004\",\"schema_version\":\"exact-action-result-v0\",\"tool\":\"response\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read\",\"path\":\"test/deployment-waves.test.mjs\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nEXACT ACTION RESULT\n{\"accepted\":true,\"bytes\":1176,\"candidate_id\":\"2fc2be00c2187276656bd1cade8253893a6b784ac98e6df87ee36f8075d335bb\",\"content\":\"import assert from \\\"node:assert/strict\\\";\\nimport test from \\\"node:test\\\";\\n\\nimport { describeWave, listServiceIds, planDeploymentWaves } from \\\"../src/deployment-waves.mjs\\\";\\n\\ntest(\\\"preserved helpers retain their behavior\\\", () => {\\n  assert.deepEqual(listServiceIds([{ id: \\\"api\\\" }, { id: \\\"web\\\" }]), [\\\"api\\\", \\\"web\\\"]);\\n  assert.equal(describeWave([\\\"api\\\", \\\"web\\\"]), \\\"api+web\\\");\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"dependency closure creates strictly later dependent waves\\\", () => {\\n  const result = planDeploymentWaves([\\\" web \\\"], [\\n    { id: \\\"db\\\", priority: 1 },\\n    { id: \\\"api\\\", dependsOn: [\\\"db\\\"], priority: 5 },\\n    { id: \\\"web\\\", dependsOn: [\\\"api\\\"], priority: 9 }\\n  ], { maxParallel: 3 });\\n  assert.deepEqual(result, {\\n    requestedIds: [\\\"web\\\"],\\n    includedIds: [\\\"db\\\", \\\"api\\\", \\\"web\\\"],\\n    alreadySatisfiedIds: [],\\n    waves: [[\\\"db\\\"], [\\\"api\\\"], [\\\"web\\\"]]\\n  });\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"parallel limit and exclusive groups shape ready work\\\", () => {\\n  const result = planDeploymentWaves([\\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\", \\\"c\\\"], [\\n    { id: \\\"a\\\", priority: 9, exclusiveGroup: \\\"zone\\\" },\\n    { id: \\\"b\\\", priority: 8, exclusiveGroup: \\\"zone\\\" },\\n    { id: \\\"c\\\", priority: 7 }\\n  ], { maxParallel: 2 });\\n  assert.deepEqual(result.waves, [[\\\"a\\\", \\\"c\\\"], [\\\"b\\\"]]);\\n});\\n\\n\",\"file_sha256\":\"845674ded7512c907e14